**GRAPPLE — clarified persistence**

- When GRAPPLE resolves, it designates an **original target** (the defender if you attacked, the attacker if you defended).
- That original target gains Rooted.
- As long as **you** remain Anchored, the Rooted continues to apply to that same original target on subsequent turns. It does not jump to whoever happens to be attacking or defending you later.
- Anchored is the voluntary condition you maintain (by not moving) to keep the effect alive. It functions as a self-imposed Rooted that you can choose to end by moving, at which point the ongoing Rooted on the original target also ends.

So the card creates a lasting lock on one specific person, sustained by your own willingness to stay put.

RED — BODY
